.TH UMBRA 1 "2026-09-18" "umbra 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
umbra \- one-toggle privacy/anonymity/hardening posture engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B umbra
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B umbra
reconciles a Linux machine to a declarative privacy posture (a
.IR profile )
and can restore it exactly. Each change is snapshotted before it is applied, so
any posture can be cleanly undone \(em even after a crash.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List available profiles.
.TP
.B status \fR[\fIprofile\fR]
Show measured posture versus a profile (default: home).
.TP
.B plan \fIprofile\fR
Show the actions an apply would take (no changes).
.TP
.B apply \fIprofile\fR
Reconcile the machine to a profile. Fail-mode=closed profiles need \fB--confirm\fR.
.TP
.B normal
Restore to stock by replaying the active transaction's snapshots.
.TP
.B restore \fR[\fB--tx\fI ID\fR]
Restore a transaction (default: the current one).
.TP
.B audit \fR[\fIprofile\fR] [\fB--html\fI PATH\fR]
Read-only proof of posture; optionally write an HTML dashboard.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dry-run
Show mutations without performing them.
.TP
.B --json
Machine-readable output where supported.
.TP
.B --confirm
Acknowledge a fail-mode=closed apply.
.TP
.B --pkexec
Re-run the command as root via pkexec (a desktop authentication dialog) instead
of sudo, using the polkit action com.forrestlasiter.umbra.run.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/umbra
Installed code, profiles, and schema.
.TP
.I /var/lib/umbra/transactions
Snapshot transactions used for restore.
.TP
.I /etc/umbra/boot-profile
Profile applied at boot by umbra-boot.service.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; non-zero on failure or verification failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation: https://github.com/ForrestLasiter/umbra
